user.t:
You are hive agent "vector-lab" (a ruflo vector-engineer) in a hybrid hive. Read: C:[REDACTED:high_entropy].md, LLM-DESIGN.md, BUS.md (all of it, especially the queen's vector directive), cartographer.md and router-trainer.md.
Peers you can coordinate with via BUS.md: ingestor (data pipeline), llm-smith (local LLM), mesh-coder (neural-mesh router), ecosystem-scout, sona-trainer. Post on BUS.md before touching anything shared.
Task: decide what ruvector (npm, NOT quarantined, so you may install and run it) can add to C:/Users/mariu/neural-mesh and C:/Users/mariu/hebbian-router. Look at:
(1) its vector database / HNSW / RVF containers (lineage, derive, compact) as the mesh's memory store, or alongside it. Can ruvector's memory become the mesh's memory? Compare it with neural-mesh's own store, which already has int8/PCA192, HNSW and a tested sync, on recall@k, latency, size and durability;
(2) GNN layers / differentiable search;
(3) attention mechanisms (MoE, hyperbolic, local-global) as routing or retrieval features;
(4) hooks: error-record/suggest (error→fix pairs), coedit, trajectories, rag-context, as sources of learning signals from agent work.
Use a scratch install under C:[REDACTED:high_entropy] (ruvector 0.2.25 is installed there). Known bug: `embed` fails (onnx/pkg lacks files, and the add-on is CommonJS), so get 384-d MiniLM vectors from neural-mesh's Rust encoder instead. Also check for a newer ruvector release that fixes embed.
For each candidate, follow the hive gate: hypothesis → measured comparison on the repo's own benchmark (neural-mesh: py/b1 battery for retrieval/memory, src/bin/experiment.rs for routing; hebbian-router: `node src/experiment.js` plus `--heldout`) → KEEP only on a significant paired win with no regression and all tests green; otherwise revert and log it as a negative. Integration must be opt-in. Commit winners locally by explicit path (neural-mesh: coordinate src/ edits with mesh-coder and llm-smith on BUS.md first; never touch their files).
Return ≤ 30 lines: each candidate → verdict (BREAKS / NO EFFECT / IMPROVES / NEGATIVE), with numbers (n, seeds, CI), and commits. If writing a board file is blocked, put the content in the report.
